# Frontend Rule Adapter

Read these canonical docs before editing frontend code:

- `docs/engineering/principles.md`
- `docs/engineering/frontend-svelte.md`
- `docs/engineering/coding-standards.md`
- `docs/engineering/design-system.md`
- `docs/engineering/testing.md`
- `docs/engineering/security.md` when handling user input, location, privacy, or AI behavior

Project-specific reminders:

- Use Svelte 5 with runes.
- Use Vite, not SvelteKit, unless the project explicitly changes direction.
- Use `pnpm`.
- Use CSS Modules.
- Do not use `export let`, legacy `on:` directives, Tailwind, or mixed package managers.
- Keep non-trivial logic out of `.svelte` files.
